---
description: CSS module and styling conventions (web only)
globs: "*.{css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Class names use kebab-case (`variant-fill`), never camelCase (`variantFill`)
- CSS modules (`*.module.css`) with `className` are preferred over inline `style` props
- Only use `style` for truly dynamic values (e.g. computed positions)
- CSS custom properties (`var(--color-foo)`) are web-only; mobile uses theme tokens from `@ui/common/src/theme/specifications.ts`
- Steampunk/cyber-inspired styling
